    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d326-a1-a38">

                <pb facs="0525" n="485" sameAs="frus:frus1865p1/pg485"/>

                <head>[Enclosure No. 38.]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Police Department, Superintendent’s
                                Office,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Melbourne,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-02-15"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 15, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to inform you that I
                    arrested four men last night who were making their escape from the ship
                    Shenandoah. They are now in the watch-house at Williamstown, and I shall feel
                    obliged by your sending Madden, or some other person, who may possibly be able
                    to identify them.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>THOMAS LYTTLETON, <hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Superintendent.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">William Blanchard,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">American Consul</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
